-- title:
--   Separability of j(q^N) over K(j) in good characteristic
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, let $N$ be a positive natural number, let $\ell$ be a prime, assume $K$ has characteristic $\ell$, and assume $\ell \nmid N$. Work inside the field $K(\!(q)\!)$ of formal Laurent series over $K$, realised as Hahn series over $\mathbb{Z}$. Write $j_q =$ `jqModC K` for the element $q^{-1}$ (the Hahn series with single coefficient $1$ in degree $-1$) multiplied by the power series obtained from $\mathrm{jNum} = E_4^3 \cdot \eta^{-1}\text{-unit}$, i.e. `eisenstein4 ^ 3 * dedekindEtaUnitInv`, by base change along $\mathbb{Z} \to K$; and write $j_{q^N} =$ `jqNModC K N` for the image of $j_q$ under the ring homomorphism `qExpand K N`, which acts on Hahn series by the exponent dilation $n \mapsto Nn$, that is, by the substitution $q \mapsto q^N$. The conclusion is that $j_{q^N}$ is separable over the intermediate field $K(j_q)$ of $K(\!(q)\!)$ generated by $j_q$ over $K$: its minimal polynomial over that subfield is a separable polynomial.
--
--   This is Igusa's good-reduction separability statement for the level-$N$ modular equation, in the form that the degeneracy extension $K(j(q)) \subseteq K(j(q), j(q^N))$ is separable whenever the characteristic of $K$ does not divide $N$. It is the separable-generation input used downstream to see that the modular function fields in characteristic $\ell$ define curves, and is cited by the work on characteristic-$p$ models of $X_0(N)$ and on full-level models.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_isSeparable_jqNModC_of_good.lean

